  abstract = {Study region: Canada. Study focus: Given the effects of climate change on extreme precipitation, updated IntensityDuration-Frequency (IDF) relationships have been adopted across Canada. Since the IDFs’ generation is based on the assumption of stationarity, the rainfall statistics information may be unreliable. Recent research is attempting to develop a new methodology to integrate nonstationarity and climate change into IDFs updating process. Up to now, there is no comprehensive evaluation of the IDFs updating procedure at different locations. In this study, we analyzed the combined effect of non-stationarity and climate change on future IDFs at six selected gauging stations across Canada.},
